      "writtenOn": "2026-09-08T22:55:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit Premature CPU flag checks before parameter validation                                                                                         \n                                                                                                                                                        \n  In convert_from_argb.cc:1934, convert_from_argb.cc:2347, and convert_from_argb.cc:2742, the parameter check:                                          \n                                                                                                                                                        \n    if (!src_argb || !dst_y || !dst_uv || !argbconstants || width \u003c\u003d 0 ||                                                                               \n        width \u003e (INT_MAX / 2) || height \u003d\u003d 0 || height \u003d\u003d INT_MIN) {                                                                                    \n      return -1;                                                                                                                                        \n    }                                                                                                                                                   \n                                                                                                                                                        \n  is placed halfway down the function (after ARGBToYMatrixRow and ARGBToUVMatrixRow dispatch, but before Convert8To16Row, MultiplyRow_16, and           \n  MergeUVRow). Moving this check to the very start of each function avoids running unnecessary TestCpuFlag(...) calls when parameters are invalid.",
      "parentUuid": "47ff6446_02fa54c2",
